{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":2299703,"num_turns":281,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"7b20184f-7d2b-4571-a2dc-96b5f2bbff41","total_cost_usd":37.678318000000004,"usage":{"input_tokens":467,"cache_creation_input_tokens":351350,"cache_read_input_tokens":60378312,"output_tokens":158792,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":351350,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1428,"cache_read_input_tokens":366421,"cache_creation_input_tokens":197,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":197},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":3462,"outputTokens":13,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0035269999999999998,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":467,"outputTokens":158792,"cacheReadInputTokens":60378312,"cacheCreationInputTokens":351350,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":37.674791000000006,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Handed off to review. `TASK-260720-1ljev5` is at `to-review`, checklist 9/9.\n\n## What landed\n\nWorktree: `.temp/TASK-260720-1ljev5/worktree`, composed from the accepted `TASK-260720-2284br` tree (`.temp/TASK-260720-1zntv0/worktree`, base `origin/main` 17804ce). Nothing staged, committed, or published. Task-only delta is 15 files.\n\n**`internal/buildcache/collect.go`** — `Sweep` under a caller-held home lock. It removes an entry only when every proof holds: cache root revalidates as protected state via the new `openProtectedDir` (no link or reparse point followed at any component, owner and mode/DACL checked, handle held open for the whole sweep); the name is exactly 64 lowercase hex; no marker or journal references it; the entry itself revalidates as protected, structurally exact, and self-consistent; and it is older than grace. Everything else is retained with an actionable warning.\n\nThe key design point: **provenance is the protected boundary, never the receipt**. The receipt is read only to learn which input the entry *claims*; that input is independently re-derived into a key that must equal the directory name, then the existing full inspection re-checks structure, receipt, artifact hash, and size.\n\nRemoval is a rename to a private `.sweep-*` sibling of the same proven root — that rename *is* the atomic removal, and the `RemoveAll` behind it is resumable cleanup the next sweep finishes. A deletion cannot escape the cache root even when the entry holds links.\n\n**`internal/scopes/gc.go`** — one shared mark phase feeding both `CollectRuntime` (behaviour unchanged) and the new `Collect`. Runtime entries are marked from every supported marker schema; build keys only from marker v2 entries that carry them plus in-flight journals — the split `TASK-260720-17llva`'s verdict required. An unreadable marker, skill directory, or consumer registry makes the reference set unprovable, so the build sweep is skipped entirely and reported.\n\n**Wiring** — `install` post-commit maintenance now runs on the same held lock and reads `Journal.ReferencedBuildKeys` first; `curator gc` acquires the home lock, recovers incomplete transactions, then collects.\n\n**Grace period** is a documented 24h constant, not a config key — the protocol config schema is closed, and the contract only says \"the manager's documented grace period\". Documented in `README.md`.\n\n## Gates\n\nmacOS: `gofmt`, `git diff --check`, `go build`, `go vet`, `go test ./... -count=1` (40 packages), four race gates, and pinned `golangci-lint` v2.4.0 repo-wide — all **exit 0**, lint reports **0 issues**. Cross-build for Windows and Linux exit 0.\n\nOne expected red, reported as such: `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` exits **1** on `internal/runtimestore/targets_windows_test.go:97: undefined: decodeHelperOutput` — pre-existing and sibling-owned; the untouched accepted base reproduces it identically. Excluding that package the gate exits 0.\n\nNative Windows needed a detour worth knowing: an elevated SSH session makes Windows own every created object as `BUILTIN\\Administrators`, which the protected-state check correctly rejects — that's the limitation `TASK-260720-1zntv0` recorded. Re-running through a temporary non-elevated `schtasks /rl LIMITED` task (deleted afterwards) gives real coverage: **every new sweep test passes natively**, `internal/scopes` and the `cmd/curator` gc serialization tests exit 0. The three remaining `internal/buildcache` failures are reproduced by the accepted base binary in the same session.\n\n## Flagged for follow-up\n\nA `consumers.json` that exists but does not parse makes `LoadConsumers` return nil, and `CollectRuntime` then rewrites the registry as empty — one corrupt file deregisters every checkout. That is established runtime GC behaviour and this task required runtime compatibility, so I left it alone; the new build sweep treats it as an uncertainty and refuses to sweep. It is in the logbook and the notes as pending its own task.","ttft_ms":1696,"ttft_stream_ms":1179,"time_to_request_ms":16,"type":"result","duration_ms":3169860,"uuid":"edd10b93-5d0f-48f0-9495-23f0b655f514"}
